    <item>
      <title>Top 4 Ways to Document a kwargs Parameter in Python</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/top-4-ways-to-document-kwargs-in-python/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 15 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/top-4-ways-to-document-kwargs-in-python/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;question&#34;&gt;Question:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Are you grappling with how to effectively document a &lt;code&gt;**kwargs&lt;/code&gt; parameter when using &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.sphinx-doc.org&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Sphinx&lt;/a&gt;&#xA; for generating API documentation in Python? While you may easily document regular parameters, &lt;code&gt;**kwargs&lt;/code&gt; can be particularly tricky. Here, I will explore several approaches to clearly document these parameters.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;solution-1-classic-approach&#34;&gt;Solution 1: Classic Approach&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here’s a basic method for documenting &lt;code&gt;**kwargs&lt;/code&gt; that has been validated for Sphinx compatibility:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;example_function&lt;/span&gt;(first, second&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;two&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;**&lt;/span&gt;kwargs):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;Fetches and returns a value.&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    :param first: The first parameter&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    :type first: ``int``&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    :param second: The second parameter&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    :type second: ``str``&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    :param **kwargs: Additional keyword arguments.&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    :Keyword Arguments:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    * *extra* (``list``) -- Additional items&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    * *supplement* (``dict``) -- Extra content needed&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    &amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this example, the use of &lt;code&gt;r&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot; ... &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt; enables the docstring to preserve raw formatting, ensuring the &lt;code&gt;*&lt;/code&gt; is treated as a literal character, which is essential for Sphinx to process it correctly. The use of a bulleted list helps maintain consistency with the parameters section provided by Sphinx documentation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
